## Expert Summary

Farzana Hasan, [diamond expert](/about-farzana/) at DiamondCritics, has evaluated hundreds of [men's diamond rings](/mens-diamond-rings) across budget tiers, hand sizes, and occupations.

Picking a men's diamond ring comes down to sequence, not preference. Most regret happens when men jump to a stone they saw online and then try to build backward — finding a setting that fits, then discovering the total is wrong for their budget or the setting is wrong for their hands.

The correct sequence is budget → occupation → metal → setting → stone. Each step narrows the field. By step 5, there are two or three correct options, not two hundred.

The single most underrated variable is occupation. A ring that is correct for a finance professional in an office can be damaged and unwearable within six months on a construction worker's hand. Get this right before anything else.

